Under “background-clip: text”, Ladybird clips the background to the
glyphs and the decoration lines of the text, both painted opaque. Blink
does the same: Its TextDecorationPainter::LineColorForPhase() paints the
lines black in PaintPhase::kTextClip, behind the feature flag
BackgroundClipTextDecoration, as its TextPainter does the glyphs. And
WebKit’s TextBoxPainter paints the decorations in every phase but
PaintPhase::Selection, so its TextClip phase takes them in too. Gecko
leaves them out: Chrome 158 and WebKit 26.5 show the background through
the lines of WPT’s clip-text-text-decorations.html, while Firefox 151
shows it through the glyphs alone.
